											<table border="0" cellPadding="1" cellSpacing="1" width="100%">
											                        
												<!--Insert News here -->
												<tr><td class=RowHeading align=middle>May 4, 2001</td></tr><tr><td background="images/redline.gif" height=4></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsSubHead><a name="33"><strong>Guildie Of The Month - April</strong><br><font SIZE=2>Submitted by:&nbsp;</font><a href="feadorn@clemmonsconsulting.com"><font COLOR=#FF0000 SIZE=2>Feadorn Lifegiver</font></a></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsText>Grongl has been selected for Guildie of the Month for the month of Arpil.  He has went above and beyond the call of duty on every raid he as been on. Congrats Grongl and keep up the good work!<br><br>
<p align=middle>
<img SRC="images\GronglLg.jpg"><br>
</p></td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=NewsSubHead><a name="32"><strong>New Patch On May 8th</strong><br><font SIZE=2>Submitted by:&nbsp;</font><a href="feadorn@clemmonsconsulting.com"><font COLOR=#FF0000 SIZE=2>Feadorn Lifegiver</font></a></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsText>
On Tuesday, May 8th, at 3AM PST (10AM GMT), all servers will be brought down for a scheduled patch. The estimated downtime is 9 hours. <br><br>
- The EverQuest Team

</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=RowHeading align=middle>May 3, 2001</td></tr><tr><td background="images/redline.gif" height=4></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsSubHead><a name="31"><strong>More Info On Luclin</strong><br><font SIZE=2>Submitted by:&nbsp;</font><a href="feadorn@clemmonsconsulting.com"><font COLOR=#FF0000 SIZE=2>Feadorn Lifegiver</font></a></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsText>This information was taken from eqcastersrealm.
<blockquote>
Some details are coming in from people who have received the recent publication of CGW which contained details on the new Shadows of Luclin expansion. 
<br><br>
Here are some preliminary facts:
<br><UL>
<li>The new graphics models will allow for facial expression when you are angry, surprised, scared, etc.</li> 
<li>You will be able to access Luclin from the wizard spires and platforms. Not sure yet if it will be Wizard only or not though. </li>
<li>The Beastlord will be a Shaman / Warrior hybrid. It is described as 'the first class that can tank and conjure a pet' (this is CGW's words not ours or SOE's). </li>
<li>The pet you conjure can zone with you as you go from one zone to the next. </li>
<li>A zone will be set up specific as a Bazaar. This will be a formal area to buy and sell without all the shouting. </li>
<li>The new race will be 'good' in alignment. </li>
<li>Half the world will always be in dark and half in the light. You will also be able to travel through the core of the moon where there will be cities and dungeons. </li>
</blockquote></td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=RowHeading align=middle>May 2, 2001</td></tr><tr><td background="images/redline.gif" height=4></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsSubHead><a name="30"><strong>What happens when Instill Doubt fails!</strong><br><font SIZE=2>Submitted by:&nbsp;</font><a href="feadorn@clemmonsconsulting.com"><font COLOR=#FF0000 SIZE=2>Feadorn Lifegiver</font></a></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsText>Here is a video clip that was sent in by Ssakk.  It is entitled: "What happens when Instill Doubt fails!"  Take a look: <br><br>

<a href="TeasingCat.mpg">When Install Doubt Fails!</a></td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=RowHeading align=middle>April 26, 2001</td></tr><tr><td background="images/redline.gif" height=4></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsSubHead><a name="29"><strong>EzBoard Migration Update</strong><br><font SIZE=2>Submitted by:&nbsp;</font><a href="feadorn@clemmonsconsulting.com"><font COLOR=#FF0000 SIZE=2>Feadorn Lifegiver</font></a></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsText>This was a message posted by the EzBoard team:
<blockquote>
Well, we were able to do successfully move our entire operations over to another managed services facility. You should already be seeing improved performance. 
<br><br>
This new facility will allow us to grow and provide more reliable service in the long term. Considering that we had only two weeks of notice to sign a contract and move our operations, I think we did extremely well.
<br><br>
We know that for some of you, the down time was a little longer than expected, but we assure you that it was absolutely necessary and it will be well worth it.
<br><br>
At this point in time, we will continue to mop up any remaining issues and leverage the relationship with our new provider (XUMA) to improve our services even more.
<br><br>
We thank you for your patience and understanding.
<br><br>
- the ezboard team 
</blockquote></td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=NewsSubHead><a name="28"><strong>Shadows of Luclin Now Online</strong><br><font SIZE=2>Submitted by:&nbsp;</font><a href="feadorn@clemmonsconsulting.com"><font COLOR=#FF0000 SIZE=2>Feadorn Lifegiver</font></a></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsText>The Everquest site <a href="http://everquest.station.sony.com/luclin/index.jsp" target=_new>Shadows of Luclin</a> is now on line.  It has a few screen shots as well as a look at the new character models.  It also says that other shamanize races may be allowed to create the new Beastmaster class.  Click on the link above to go visit it.</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=RowHeading align=middle>April 25, 2001</td></tr><tr><td background="images/redline.gif" height=4></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsSubHead><a name="27"><strong>EzBoard Network Glitches</strong><br><font SIZE=2>Submitted by:&nbsp;</font><a href="feadorn@clemmonsconsulting.com"><font COLOR=#FF0000 SIZE=2>Feadorn Lifegiver</font></a></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsText>There is a message from EzBoard about the performance of the boards:
<br>
<blockquote>
We are currently experience network glitches. We appreciate your patience while we investigate the performance problems.
</blockquote>
It will sometimes work and sometimes not.  </td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=NewsSubHead><a name="23"><strong>Happenings On The Test Server</strong><br><font SIZE=2>Submitted by:&nbsp;</font><a href="feadorn@clemmonsconsulting.com"><font COLOR=#FF0000 SIZE=2>Feadorn Lifegiver</font></a></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsText>Two interesting items on the Test Server currently: 
<ul> 
<li><b>Traveller Boots:</b> These are a slightly less effective form of Journeyman Boots.  They cost between 5200 and 7000pp depending on your Charisma, from the Tinker Bag NPC in Solusek A.  Unlike Journeyman Boots they have a casting time (you can't click on the run).
<BR><BR>Note that the speed of the boots is the same as Journeyman Boots (which is significantly slower than an alchemy made Spirit of Wolf potion). <BR></li> 
<br><li><b>Lure of Insects:</b>  This is a new Shaman only slow spell on test.  It is a magic based lure spell which is <u>much</u> less resisted on higher level NPC's.  The slow is only 25%, but that is still very significant on mobs which could not be slowed otherwise.</li> </ul> 
As always these are currently only on test and may change before going live, or not go live at all. <br><br>
Note: This story was taken from eqcastersrealm.	</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=NewsSubHead><a name="22"><strong>Shadows Of Luclin</strong><br><font SIZE=2>Submitted by:&nbsp;</font><a href="feadorn@clemmonsconsulting.com"><font COLOR=#FF0000 SIZE=2>Feadorn Lifegiver</font></a></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsText>Bits of information on the upcoming expansion  Shadows of Luclin. 
<br><br>
<blockquote>
Yes, other races will be able to become Beastlords, but there are certain limitations involved.
</blockquote>
Head to this <a href="http://boards.station.sony.com/ubb/everquest/Forum1/HTML/000109.html">link</a> for more. </td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=RowHeading align=middle>April 24, 2001</td></tr><tr><td background="images/redline.gif" height=4></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsSubHead><a name="21"><strong>Message Boards Are Down!</strong><br><font SIZE=2>Submitted by:&nbsp;</font><a href="feadorn@clemmonsconsulting.com"><font COLOR=#FF0000 SIZE=2>Feadorn Lifegiver</font></a></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsText>The message boards are down due to maint.  Here is the message from EzBoard: <br><blockquote>Today, April 24th, from 9:00 AM PST to 6:00 PM PST, we are moving all ezboards to our new, much faster bandwidth provider. During this time all ezboards will be unavailable. Following the move all ezboards will experience a dramatic increase in speed. 


We appreciate your patience during this downtime. Please feel free to read our newest ezboard newsletter while you wait. </blockquote>

</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=RowHeading align=middle>April 19, 2001</td></tr><tr><td background="images/redline.gif" height=4></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsSubHead><a name="20"><strong>Web Site</strong><br><font SIZE=2>Submitted by:&nbsp;</font><a href="feadorn@clemmonsconsulting.com"><font COLOR=#FF0000 SIZE=2>Feadorn Lifegiver</font></a></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsText>This is the beginning of a new web site for ADD.  There are things that still need to be completed but I thought it was time to move to a no banner site.  
<br><br>
Thanks,<br>
Feadorn Lifegiver<br>
Level 36 Cleric<br>
<br></td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=RowHeading align=middle>April 17, 2001</td></tr><tr><td background="images/redline.gif" height=4></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsSubHead><a name="19"><strong>First Level 60 Members!!!!!!</strong><br><font SIZE=2>Submitted by:&nbsp;</font><a href="feadorn@clemmonsconsulting.com"><font COLOR=#FF0000 SIZE=2>Feadorn Lifegiver</font></a></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsText>We should take a moment and congratulate Blackpaw and Banelion both are now level 60.  This is a great accomplishment.  They now have plenty of time to power level us lower level folks :)</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=RowHeading align=middle>March 8, 2001</td></tr><tr><td background="images/redline.gif" height=4></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsSubHead><a name="15"><strong>Member Status</strong><br><font SIZE=2>Submitted by:&nbsp;</font><a href="feadorn@clemmonsconsulting.com"><font COLOR=#FF0000 SIZE=2>Feadorn Lifegiver</font></a></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsText>Please look at the members page and if your information is incorrect, please post the updated info on the message board.  Or, you can click on my name and send me an email with the info.  <BR><BR>Sorry for the slow updates recently, I am currently working on version 2 of the website and hopefully the new site will work much better.</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=RowHeading align=middle>February 27, 2001</td></tr><tr><td background="images/redline.gif" height=4></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsSubHead><a name="14"><strong>Site Updates</strong><br><font SIZE=2>Submitted by:&nbsp;</font><a href="feadorn@clemmonsconsulting.com"><font COLOR=#FF0000 SIZE=2>Feadorn Lifegiver</font></a></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsText>I have updated the members pages to reflect all of the recent activity.  For everyones information, we have 109 active members listed and 131 twinks in the guild.  I have also updated the events pages to reflect the new raids going on.  I wont add any raids to the list until there has been a date assigned to it.
<br><br>
Thank you,<br>
Feadorn Lifegiver <br>
Level 35 Cleric of Rodcet Nife<br>
Officer of At Deaths Door</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=RowHeading align=middle>February 23, 2001</td></tr><tr><td background="images/redline.gif" height=4></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsSubHead><a name="13"><strong>Quellious Quarters Closes Down</strong><br><font SIZE=2>Submitted by:&nbsp;</font><a href="feadorn@clemmonsconsulting.com"><font COLOR=#FF0000 SIZE=2>Feadorn Lifegiver</font></a></td></tr><tr><td class=NewsText>Quellious Quarters has decided to close up shop and disband.  This in affect changes our server to a FFA system when it comes to dragons and planes.  Sharac made this post on the Everlore website:
<br>
<blockquote>
QQ was deleted due to the fact that Quell seems to prefer the FFA system over the Reservation System. In addition, we are tired. Tired of the flaming, tired of the accusations against us. We have taken 14 long months of it and several of us have had to give up a game we loved because of it. We dont see any point in continuing either the site boards or the message boards at this point.
<br><br>
It was not an easy decision but one that we needed to make. I am truly sorry but I hope you can understand.
</blockquote></td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr>	

